<section id="section-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">Best Photo Spots in Paris at Christmas</h2>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">1. Dior, Avenue Montaigne</h3>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={diorChristmas} alt="The Dior storefront decorated for Christmas on Avenue Montaigne in Paris" caption="Dior’s Christmas decorations on Avenue Montaigne" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={diorChristmas2} alt="A close-up of Dior's Christmas decorations on Avenue Montaigne in Paris" caption="Dior Christmas lights on Avenue Montaigne in the evening" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>One of the prettiest Christmas photo spots in Paris. Go in the afternoon, when the lights start to come on and Dior looks even more impressive.</p>
    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">2. Chanel, Rue Cambon</h3>
    <ArticleImage src={chanelChristmas} alt="The Chanel storefront decorated with a giant lit bow for Christmas in Paris" caption="Chanel’s Christmas bow on Rue Cambon" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    <p>Another Instagrammable Christmas photo spot is the iconic Chanel storefront on Rue Cambon, which looks even more magical at Christmas when the lights are on.</p>
    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">3. Le Village Royal</h3>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={villageRoyal1} alt="A giant lit teddy bear Christmas decoration at Le Village Royal in Paris" caption="The Christmas teddy bear at Le Village Royal" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={villageRoyal2} alt="Lit balloon and teddy bear Christmas decorations at Le Village Royal in Paris" caption="Festive decorations at Le Village Royal" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>A little Parisian gem that gets a beautiful Christmas makeover. Definitely worth stopping by if you’re looking for something a little different.</p>
    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">4. Place Vendôme</h3>
    <ArticleImage src={placeVendome} alt="Giant Christmas trees at Place Vendôme in Paris" caption="Christmas trees at Place Vendôme" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    <p>Place Vendôme feels very Parisian and especially magical at Christmas, with its beautiful Christmas trees and lights. You can combine your visit with a stop at the Ritz Paris for a hot chocolate.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-4" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <GetYourGuideCity locationId="16" />
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">Best Hot Chocolate in Paris</h2>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>You can’t really visit Paris in winter without having a proper hot chocolate at least once. I tried quite a few during my Christmas trip, but these are the four places I enjoyed the most — including a couple of unexpected favorites.</p>
    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">1. Carette</h3>
    <ArticleImage src={carretteHotChocolate} alt="Hot chocolate from Carette in front of the Arc de Triomphe" caption="Hot chocolate from Carette" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    <p>Carette is one of my favorite places for hot chocolate in Paris. It was actually the first place where I ever tried hot chocolate in Paris, so there was no way I was going to skip it on my second visit.</p>
    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">2. Angelina</h3>
    <ArticleImage src={angelinaHotChocolate} alt="Hot chocolate and a pastry at Angelina in Paris" caption="Hot chocolate at Angelina" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    <p>Angelina is probably one of the most talked-about places for hot chocolate in Paris, and opinions are definitely divided. Some call it too touristy because of the long queues, while others swear it’s the best in Paris. Personally, I really enjoyed it — it was exactly the rich, indulgent hot chocolate I expected from a classic Parisian spot.</p>
    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">3. Ritz Paris</h3>
    <ArticleImage src={ritzHotChocolate} alt="Hot chocolate cups from the Ritz Paris Christmas pop-up" caption="Hot chocolate at the Ritz Paris" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    <p>I actually decided to try the hot chocolate at the Ritz because of its Christmas pop-up. The festive setup is adorable, with hot chocolate, marshmallows and little teddy bears that you can even take home as a souvenir — and yes, the hot chocolate was just as good as I hoped.</p>
    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">4. Lindt</h3>
    <p>Okay, I know Lindt isn’t exactly a traditional Parisian hot chocolate spot, but hear me out. Lindt has always been one of my favorite chocolate brands, and trying their hazelnut hot chocolate for the first time was honestly heavenly.</p>
  </div>
</section>

