<section id="section-8" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">FAQ</h2>
  </div>
  <div class={`${prose} space-y-6`}>
    <div id="faq-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h3 class="mb-2 text-black">1. Is Christmas in Paris worth it?</h3>
      <p>Absolutely. Paris is beautiful any time of year, but I honestly think Christmas gives the city something extra. The Christmas lights, decorated streets and shop windows, cozy cafés and festive atmosphere make you experience Paris in a completely different way. I was a little worried that I wouldn’t feel the same way about the city after almost nine years, but visiting at Christmas actually made me fall in love with Paris all over again. So, if you love Christmas as much as I do, I’d definitely say it’s worth it.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h3 class="mb-2 text-black">2. Is Christmas in Paris expensive?</h3>
      <p>It can be, especially if you’re visiting during the busiest part of December. Accommodation and popular experiences can get more expensive around Christmas, so I’d recommend booking in advance if you already know your dates. That said, you don’t need to spend a lot of money to enjoy Christmas in Paris. Walking around the beautifully decorated streets, visiting the Christmas markets and seeing the lights are some of my favorite things to do, and they don’t cost much — or anything at all.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h3 class="mb-2 text-black">3. When does Christmas in Paris start?</h3>
      <p>There isn’t one exact date when Christmas starts in Paris. You’ll usually start seeing Christmas decorations, lights and festive displays around the city from November, with more and more places getting into the Christmas spirit as December approaches. The exact timing can vary from one place to another, especially when it comes to department stores, Christmas markets and individual decorations.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h3 class="mb-2 text-black">4. When do Christmas markets in Paris start?</h3>
      <p>The Christmas markets in Paris don’t all start on the same date, so it really depends on which ones you want to visit. Some open in November, while others start later in the season. For example, the Tuileries Christmas Market starts on November 15 in 2026, while the Notre-Dame Christmas Market starts on November 26. If you have a specific market in mind, I’d recommend checking its dates before your trip, as they can change from year to year.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

